-------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE OF THE ABOVE, AND ORIGIN OF THE PATCH CONTENT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT terms above apply to the original work in this repository:

  build.py
  README.md
  docs/ANALYSIS.md
  the screenshots

They do NOT purport to license the modifications encoded in the patch files
themselves:

  dq5-4party-dejap-fixed-v1.bps
  dq5-4party-dejap-fixed-v1.ips

Those patches carry the substance of the original Japanese four-party hack by
Mr. 45, released in 2007 ("DQ5 4-person party beta", ver 1.4) and available at
https://w.atwiki.jp/dq_binary/pages/31.html . The contribution made here is a
correction to how that work was aligned when converted to the DeJap English
translation, together with a decision to omit six Japanese-layout menu edits.
That correction does not make the underlying hack anyone else's work.

Mr. 45 released his hack freely to the romhacking community. These corrected
patches are distributed in the same spirit: freely, at no charge, for people
who own the game. If Mr. 45 or any rights holder objects to this distribution,
it will be taken down on request.

An intermediate conversion of that hack to the DeJap translation was released
in 2022 by AustNerevar. No code or patch data from that release is reproduced
here; it was used only as a subject of comparison in diagnosing the alignment
error described in docs/ANALYSIS.md.

NO ROM DATA IS INCLUDED OR DISTRIBUTED IN THIS REPOSITORY. The patches contain
only the differences between two ROM images, and cannot be used without a copy
of the game that you provide yourself.
